# Git Command Cheat Sheet

## Repository Initialization
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git init` | Initialize a new repo |
| `git clone <url>` | Clone a repo |
| `git clone <url> myproject` | Clone into a specific folder |

## Configuration
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git config --global user.name "John Doe"` | Set username |
| `git config --global user.email "john@example.com"` | Set email |
| `git config --list` | View configuration |
| `git config --global credential.helper manager` | Configure credential manager |

## Status
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git status` | Shows modified, staged, and untracked files |

## Staging (Add)
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git add index.html` | Add one file |
| `git add file1.txt file2.txt` | Add multiple files |
| `git add .` | Add everything |

## Commit
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git commit -m "message"` | Commit staged files |
| `git commit -am "message"` | Add tracked changes + commit (doesn't add new files) |

## Log / History
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git log` | Full commit history |
| `git log --oneline` | Compact history |
| `git log --graph --oneline --all` | Graph view |

## Diff
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git diff` | Working dir vs last commit |
| `git diff --cached` | Staged changes vs last commit |
| `git diff abc123 def456` | Compare two commits |

## Branching
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git branch` | List branches |
| `git branch feature-login` | Create branch |
| `git checkout feature-login` / `git switch feature-login` | Switch branch |
| `git checkout -b feature-login` / `git switch -c feature-login` | Create + switch |
| `git branch -d feature-login` | Delete branch |
| `git branch -D feature-login` | Force delete branch |

## Merge
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git merge feature-login` | Merge branch into current |

## Remotes
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git remote -v` | View remotes |
| `git remote add origin <url>` | Add remote |
| `git remote remove origin` | Remove remote |
| `git remote rename origin github` | Rename remote |

## Push
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git push -u origin main` | Push first time (sets upstream) |
| `git push` | Push subsequent times |
| `git push origin feature-login` | Push another branch |

## Pull / Fetch
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git pull` | Download + merge |
| `git pull origin main` | Pull specific branch |
| `git fetch` | Download only, no merge |
| `git fetch origin` | Fetch specific remote |

## Restore / Reset / Revert
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git restore app.js` | Restore file from last commit not for un tracked files|
| `git restore --staged app.js` | Unstage a file |
| `git reset --soft HEAD~1` | Undo commit, keep changes staged |
| `git reset HEAD~1` | Undo commit, keep changes unstaged |
| `git reset --hard HEAD~1` | Undo commit, discard changes |
| `git revert HEAD` | Undo commit safely (new commit) |

## Stash
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git stash` | Save changes |
| `git stash list` | View stashes |
| `git stash pop` | Restore + delete stash |
| `git stash apply` | Restore without deleting |

## Tags
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git tag v1.0` | Create lightweight tag |
| `git tag -a v1.0 -m "Version 1.0"` | Create annotated tag |
| `git push origin --tags` | Push tags |

## Show / Inspect
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git show` | Show latest commit |
| `git show abc123` | Show specific commit |
| `git branch --show-current` | Current branch name |
| `git rev-parse HEAD` | Current commit hash |
| `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` | Repository root path |

## Remove / Move Files
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git rm file.txt` | Delete tracked file |
| `git rm --cached secrets.txt` | Stop tracking, keep local file untracked|
| `git mv old.txt new.txt` | Rename/move file |

## Clean
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git clean -f` | Delete untracked files |
| `git clean -fd` | Delete untracked files + folders |

## Cherry-pick / Rebase
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git cherry-pick abc123` | Copy a single commit |
| `git rebase main` | Rebase current branch onto main |
| `git rebase -i HEAD~5` | Interactive rebase (last 5 commits) |

## Bisect
```
git bisect start
git bisect bad
git bisect good abc123
```
Automatically binary-searches history to find the commit that introduced a bug.

## Reflog
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git reflog` | See all HEAD movements |
| `git reset --hard HEAD@{2}` | Recover a "lost" commit |

## Archive / Blame / Grep
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git archive --format=zip HEAD -o project.zip` | Create a ZIP of the repo |
| `git blame app.js` | See who changed each line |
| `git grep "login"` | Search inside repo |

## Worktree / Submodule
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `git worktree add ../feature feature-login` | Create another working directory |
| `git submodule add <url>` | Add a submodule |
| `git submodule update --init` | Update submodules |

## .gitignore Example
```
node_modules/
.env
dist/
*.log
```

---

## Typical Daily Workflow
```bash
git clone https://github.com/user/project.git
cd project

git switch -c feature-login

# Edit files...
git status
git add .
git commit -m "Add login feature"

git pull origin main
git push -u origin feature-login
```

These commands cover the vast majority of day-to-day Git work. More advanced topics — hooks, sparse checkouts, history filtering, and plumbing commands — build on this same core toolkit.